 ],
 "checker_failure": "an output sample more than atol (2 mV) from its expected value on decision, fb_metric or slicer_in_dbg outside the unscored 1.25*tr after a change of that output",
 "semantics": "Verilog-A LRM 2.4 5.10.3.1 cross (event at the crossing within its time tolerance), 4.5.8 transition (an output starts moving at the event that changes its target; delayed transitions), 5.10.3.3 initial_step; to be recorded on Spectre",
 "conditions": {
  "alt_modules": "three modules (a combinational feedback summer, a slicer/decision register, the top); accepted provided the register reading the feedback node at a clock event sees the value from before that event, because the history nodes it reads are transition() outputs whose targets change only at that event (LRM 4.5.8); the summer has no events, so no cross-instance event order is involved",
  "alt_delayed_within_tr": "uses a 0.2*tr transport delay (at most 0.2 ns); output-changing events are at least 0.5 ns apart in the legal inputs, so every delayed change has started before the next one is scheduled and no pending transition is deleted (LRM 4.5.8)",
  "interrupted_transitions": "long-tr retargets running output ramps (rst 0.6 ns after a decision, tr = 1 ns); by the LRM 4.5.8 completion rule an interrupted transition() reaches the new value within tr of the interruption, provided the transition has zero delay, equal rise and fall times tr and a target that stays constant between events (a nonzero delay, unequal rise and fall times or queued transitions need their own analysis), so every candidate built on such a transition() is judged as in the other cases; the synthetic model that waits for the running ramp to end is rejected there; the parameter-endpoint cases and min-pulse-vss-low interrupt no ramp",
  "margin_arrival_1p2tr": "arrives after the tr deadline but before the 1.25*tr scoring start; accepted under the user-confirmed observation rule (F01 A, 2026-10-28), not a correct model",
  "original_v4_354_gold": "the four released v4:354 gold modules unchanged (same top name and ports); not written for this task: mutants.py reads the historical files byte for byte, drops their include lines and joins them; empty history reads as low, both metrics follow the live inputs and the shifted history, fb_metric has no reset path; generated only inside the repository (it reads benchmark/material/historyref)",
  "empty_history_high": "power-up and every reset load +1 into both history slots, the actual change of v4:854 neg_005_reset_preserves_history (its decision_latch.va sets the three state bits to 1 at power-up and reset; the two history bits are this candidate, the third drives the gold decision output, which this candidate keeps at vss); rejected wherever the first decision after power-up or a reset has k1 + k2 > 0, which every case has",
  "second_tap_ignored": "the feedback uses tap 1 only, the fault class of v4:854 neg_003_second_tap_ignored (missing_tap; that bundle replaced the tap-2 term by a fixed 4*d1, this candidate drops it); every case has decisions with a nonzero k2 and a full second slot",
  "slow_output_1p3tr": "every output-changing event sits on its case grid so that a scored row lies strictly inside (1.25*tr, 1.3*tr) after it: 1.275*tr in seven cases, 1.255*tr in long-tr, 1.27*tr in param-endpoints-low; there a 1.3*tr arrival misses by more than 2 mV for every change of 104 mV or more, every decision change included, except the five long-tr changes (one of them a decision change) that a reset rewrites 0.6 ns later and that have no scored row of their own",
  "taps_one_decision_old": "reset-restart changes the tap codes only inside resets, where the first decision after the reset has no feedback; isi-channel and long-tr never change them",
  "tr_floor_100p": "the output transition time is max(tr, 100 ps); identical to the reference wherever tr is 100 ps or more, so only param-endpoints-low (tr = 10 ps) and min-pulse-vss-low (tr = 40 ps) reject it, at the scored row 1.27*tr and 1.275*tr after each event",
  "decision_floor_0v": "the decision output is clamped at 0 V from below; identical to the reference wherever vss is 0 V or more, so only min-pulse-vss-low (vss = -0.5 V) rejects it",
  "clk_deglitch_0p6n": "a rising clk crossing decides only after clk has been low for at least 0.6 ns, stricter than the contract minimum of 0.5 ns; the eight earlier cases keep clk low for 0.86 ns or more before every rising crossing, so only min-pulse-vss-low (one low time of 0.502 ns) rejects it; its time comparison in the event body is far from the 0.6 ns boundary in every case",
  "all": "every expectation assumes cross() events at the crossing or just after it: within a few ps in the cases with tr of 100 ps or more, within 3 ps in min-pulse-vss-low (tr = 40 ps), where margin_arrival_1p2tr reaches its target 3 ps before the scored row 1.275*tr after the event and the reference 11 ps before it, and within 0.7 ps in param-endpoints-low (tr = 10 ps), where margin_arrival_1p2tr reaches its target 0.7 ps before the scored row 1.27*tr after the event and the reference 2.7 ps before it; vin is flat within 100 ps of every rising clk crossing and every slicer input is at least 7 mV from vcm, so the decision does not depend on the exact event time"
 },
